# 4. INTELLIGENT INTEREST SCORING

Create an individual interest profile for each fan.

Calculate interest scores using engagement signals.

Use a weighted ranking system that can evolve into machine-learning-based ranking.

### Suggested initial engagement weights

| Fan action | Signal weight |
|---|---:|
| Video watched for a long time | +5 |
| Video completed | +6 |
| Video replayed | +8 |
| Video liked | +4 |
| Video saved | +7 |
| Video shared | +7 |
| Comment posted | +5 |
| Creator profile opened | +3 |
| Creator followed | +8 |
| Creator subscribed to | +10 |
| Paid content purchased | +10 |
| Video skipped immediately | -4 |
| Explicitly selected Not Interested | -10 |
| Creator unfollowed | Negative creator preference |

These are initial values, not permanent rules.

The system must consider watch duration and completion rate rather than relying only on clicks.

For example, a fan who watches an entire video should generally generate a stronger positive signal than someone who only sees the thumbnail.

### Interest categories

Use the existing ACOVON categories and hashtags.

Build interest profiles such as:
- Favorite categories.
- Favorite hashtags.
- Favorite creators.
- Favorite content formats.
- Preferred video duration.
- Preferred viewing patterns.
- Preferred languages, when reliably available.
- Recently emerging interests.
- Categories with declining engagement.

Allow the recommendation engine to learn additional interests from content metadata and fan behavior.

