# 7. FOR YOU RANKING MODEL

Create a configurable initial ranking model.

Suggested starting weights:

| Ranking signal | Weight |
|---|---:|
| Interest and category relevance | 25% |
| Creator affinity | 20% |
| Watch time and completion | 20% |
| Engagement signals | 15% |
| Content freshness | 10% |
| Quality and popularity | 5% |
| Discovery and diversity adjustment | 5% |

These weights must be configurable through authorized administrator settings.

Negative feedback, blocked creators, reports, policy restrictions and content-access rules must override ordinary ranking signals.

The ranking system must:
- Produce different feeds for different fans.
- Refresh recommendations as new activity is collected.
- Avoid repeatedly showing the same content.
- Avoid excessive repetition from one creator.
- Mix familiar creators with new discoveries.
- Include fresh content when relevant.
- Avoid allowing popularity alone to dominate.
- Recognize content already viewed, liked, saved or purchased.
- Respect creator posting frequency and content availability.

